cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Loop heat pipe operating point — an interactive qualitative study model
message: >-
  This is a teaching model with a qualitative closure. It has not been
  validated against experiment or against a high-fidelity code. Please cite it
  as a pedagogical tool, and do not cite its numbers as physical results.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: EzukaFuya
repository-code: 'https://github.com/EzukaFuya/lhp-operating-point'
url: 'https://ezukafuya.github.io/lhp-operating-point/'
abstract: >-
  An interactive study model of a loop heat pipe, showing how the compensation
  chamber temperature sets the pressure level of the loop, how much capillary
  head remains, and whether the returning liquid can absorb the parasitic heat
  leak. It runs in two modes: a prescribed-CC calculation that reports the CC
  energy-balance residual left over, and a passive calculation that solves for
  the CC temperature at which that residual vanishes. All quantities are
  dimensionless; temperature and pressure are reduced by their critical-point
  values, and the interfacial and transport properties are normalised at a
  reference state of Tr = 0.7. The property closure is a set of shape
  functions chosen for qualitative trend fidelity, not a fit to any fluid.
keywords:
  - loop heat pipe
  - compensation chamber
  - two-phase thermal control
  - capillary limit
  - educational software
license: MIT
version: 2.3.0
date-released: '2026-08-28'
